<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f21b20ad-0a8e-5e58-855f-a93dcb088012" activityNameId="f29868d1-2343-5ec1-9beb-928409f467a5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Diesel, burned in hydraulic digger, average, with particle filter</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Diesel, burned in hydraulic digger, average, with particle filter
According to the dataset "diesel, burned in building machine, with particle filter/MJ/CH," regulated exhaust emissions are calculated using the non-road database published by BAFU (2015) for the year 2015. Emissions of CO₂, CO, CH₄, NMVOC, NOₓ, N₂O, and PM were calculated based on specific average values for hydraulic diggers and are derived from non-road emission data. Data from the Emissions Inventory Guidebook (EMEP/EEA, 2013) were used for specific exhaust emissions not covered by the non-road database. The emission factors assume that all building machines are equipped with particle filters. NMVOC speciation is modelled using the distribution shares for lorries, and noise emissions are assumed to be proportional to the fuel consumption of lorries. The consumption of lubricating oil is taken from ecoinvent v2.2. 
UUID: c6dd715e-9a38-481c-9556-b10cf8dd940c
This dataset is based on the process "diesel, burned in building machine, with particle filter/MJ/CH". Compared to this reference process, the dataset includes only lubricating oil, diesel fuel and the emissions produced during the combustion of 1 MJ of diesel fuel in an average hydraulic digger in Switzerland. The provision of the building machine is excluded.
Location: Europe
Technology: The process "diesel, burned in building machine, with particle filter/MJ/CH" has been modified to generate a dataset that consider the emissions produced during the combustion of 1 MJ of diesel fuel in a hydraulic digger in Switzerland.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Statistics
Extrapolations: Noise emissions and NMVOC speciation modelled based on data for lorries.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c6dd715e-9a38-481c-9556-b10cf8dd940c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
